{"id":"846cafe9ae25fdf6b06fbd896a533a035ce4e9aa","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"846cafe9ae25fdf6b06fbd896a533a035ce4e9aa","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/systemd-analyze.xml","lines":["@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@","       <arg choice=\"plain\">syscall-filter</arg>","       <arg choice=\"opt\"><replaceable>SET</replaceable>…</arg>","     </cmdsynopsis>","+    <cmdsynopsis>","+      <command>systemd-analyze</command>","+      <arg choice=\"opt\" rep=\"repeat\">OPTIONS</arg>","+      <arg choice=\"plain\">io-uring-filter</arg>","+      <arg choice=\"opt\"><replaceable>NAME</replaceable>…</arg>","+    </cmdsynopsis>","     <cmdsynopsis>","       <command>systemd-analyze</command>","       <arg choice=\"opt\" rep=\"repeat\">OPTIONS</arg>","@@ -600,6 +606,31 @@ Conditions succeeded.</programlisting>","       <replaceable>SET</replaceable> must include the <literal>@</literal> prefix.</para>","     </refsect2>"," ","+    <refsect2>","+      <title><command>systemd-analyze io-uring-filter <optional><replaceable>NAME</replaceable>...</optional></command></title>","+","+      <para>Lists the","+      <citerefentry project='man-pages'><refentrytitle>io_uring</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+      operations that systemd knows, or only the operations with the specified names. The names are the ones","+      that <varname>IOUringFilter=</varname> takes, see","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.exec</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>. For","+      each operation, the <literal>SYSCALLS</literal> column lists the system calls whose work the operation","+      can do. <varname>SystemCallFilter=</varname> denies an operation if it denies any of the listed system","+      calls.</para>","+","+      <example>","+        <title>Table output</title>","+        <programlisting>$ systemd-analyze io-uring-filter nop read socket uring_cmd","+NAME      SYSCALLS","+nop       -","+read      read pread64","+socket    socket","+uring_cmd ioctl setsockopt getsockopt getsockname</programlisting>","+      </example>","+","+      <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/>","+    </refsect2>","+","     <refsect2>","       <title><command>systemd-analyze filesystems <optional><replaceable>SET</replaceable>...</optional></command></title>"," "],"additions":31,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/systemd.exec.xml","lines":["@@ -2539,7 +2539,8 @@ BindReadOnlyPaths=/var/lib/systemd</programlisting>","         listed operations are denied (deny-listing). Otherwise, only the listed operations are allowed","         (allow-listing). An allow list also denies the operations of newer kernels that systemd doesn't","         know, even though the kernel reports them as supported. Operation names that systemd doesn't know","-        are ignored.</para>","+        are ignored. Use <command>systemd-analyze io-uring-filter</command> to list the operations that","+        systemd knows.</para>"," ","         <para>This option may be specified more than once, in which case the lists are merged. If the first","         assignment starts with <literal>~</literal>, the list is a deny list, otherwise it is an allow list.","@@ -3043,7 +3044,8 @@ RestrictNamespaces=~cgroup net</programlisting>","         if the filter allows <function>io_uring_setup()</function>. An operation that can do the work of","         one or more system calls, such as <constant>IORING_OP_OPENAT</constant> or","         <constant>IORING_OP_SOCKET</constant>, is denied if the filter denies any of its equivalent system","-        calls. Operations of newer kernels that systemd doesn't know are not affected. Denied requests","+        calls. <command>systemd-analyze io-uring-filter</command> lists the equivalent system calls of each","+        operation. Operations of newer kernels that systemd doesn't know are not affected. Denied requests","         always fail with <constant>EACCES</constant>, regardless of","         <varname>SystemCallErrorNumber=</varname> and of the action of the system call. System calls that","         are denied with an error number of 0 do not affect io_uring operations, since a denied request"],"additions":4,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/bash/systemd-analyze","lines":["@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@ __get_syscall_sets() {","     done"," }"," ","+__get_io_uring_ops() {","+    systemd-analyze --no-legend --no-pager io-uring-filter 2>/dev/null | { while read -r a b; do echo \" $a\"; done; }","+}","+"," __get_architectures() {","     systemd-analyze --no-legend --no-pager architectures 2>/dev/null | { while read -r a b; do echo \" $a\"; done; }"," }","@@ -88,6 +92,7 @@ _systemd_analyze() {","         [DUMP]='dump'","         [VERIFY]='verify'","         [SECCOMP_FILTER]='syscall-filter'","+        [IO_URING_FILTER]='io-uring-filter'","         [CAT_CONFIG]='cat-config'","         [SECURITY]='security'","         [CONDITION]='condition'","@@ -249,6 +254,13 @@ _systemd_analyze() {","             comps='--help --version --system --user --global --no-pager --json=off --json=pretty --json=short --table --no-legend --scale-svg --detailed'","         fi"," ","+    elif __contains_word \"$verb\" ${VERBS[IO_URING_FILTER]}; then","+        if [[ $cur = -* ]]; then","+            comps='--help --version --no-pager --json=off --json=pretty --json=short --no-legend'","+        else","+            comps=$( __get_io_uring_ops )","+        fi","+","     elif __contains_word \"$verb\" ${VERBS[ARCHITECTURES]}; then","         if [[ $cur = -* ]]; then","             comps='--help --version --no-pager --json=off --json=pretty --json=short --no-legend'"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/zsh/_systemd-analyze","lines":["@@ -43,6 +43,13 @@","         _describe -t groups 'syscall groups' _groups || compadd \"$@\"","     }"," ","+(( $+functions[_systemd-analyze_io-uring-filter] )) ||","+    _systemd-analyze_io-uring-filter() {","+        local -a _ops","+        _ops=( $(systemd-analyze --quiet --no-pager --no-legend io-uring-filter 2>/dev/null | { while read -r a b; do echo \" $a\"; done; }) )","+        _describe -t operations 'io_uring operations' _ops || compadd \"$@\"","+    }","+"," (( $+functions[_systemd-analyze_filesystems] )) ||","     _systemd-analyze_filesystems() {","         local -a _groups","@@ -95,6 +102,7 @@","             'exit-status:List known exit statuses'","             'capability:List capability definitions'","             'syscall-filter:List syscalls in seccomp filters'","+            'io-uring-filter:List io_uring operations'","             'filesystems:List known filesystems'","             'condition:Evaluate Condition*= and Assert*= assignments'","             'verify:Check unit files for correctness'"],"additions":8,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/analyze/analyze-io-uring-filter.c","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@","+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later */","+","+#include <linux/io_uring.h>","+#include <stdlib.h>","+","+#include \"analyze.h\"","+#include \"analyze-io-uring-filter.h\"","+#include \"format-table.h\"","+#include \"io-uring-filter.h\"","+#include \"log.h\"","+#include \"nulstr-util.h\"","+#include \"strv.h\"","+","+static int add_op(Table *t, int op) {","+        _cleanup_strv_free_ char **syscalls = NULL;","+        const char *s;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(t);","+","+        s = io_uring_op_syscalls_to_string(op);","+        if (s) {","+                syscalls = strv_split_nulstr(s);","+                if (!syscalls)","+                        return log_oom();","+        }","+","+        r = table_add_many(t,","+                           TABLE_INT, op,","+                           TABLE_STRING, io_uring_op_to_string(op),","+                           TABLE_STRV_WRAPPED, syscalls);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return table_log_add_error(r);","+","+        return 0;","+}","+","+int verb_io_uring_filter(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *userdata) {","+        _cleanup_(table_unrefp) Table *table = NULL;","+        int r;","+","+        table = table_new(\"opcode\", \"name\", \"syscalls\");","+        if (!table)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        (void) table_hide_column_from_display(table, (size_t) 0);","+        table_set_ersatz_string(table, TABLE_ERSATZ_DASH);","+","+        char **args = strv_skip(argv, 1);","+        if (args) {","+                STRV_FOREACH(arg, args) {","+                        int op;","+","+                        op = io_uring_op_from_string(*arg);","+                        if (op < 0)","+                                return log_error_errno(op, \"io_uring operation \\\"%s\\\" not known.\", *arg);","+","+                        r = add_op(table, op);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return r;","+                }","+","+                (void) table_set_sort(table, (size_t) 0);","+        } else","+                for (int op = 0; op < IORING_OP_LAST; op++) {","+                        r = add_op(table, op);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return r;","+                }","+","+        r = table_print_with_pager(table, arg_json_format_flags, arg_pager_flags, arg_legend);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        return EXIT_SUCCESS;","+}"],"additions":76,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/analyze/analyze-io-uring-filter.h","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later */","+#pragma once","+","+#include \"forward.h\"","+","+int verb_io_uring_filter(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *userdata);"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/analyze/analyze.c","lines":["@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@"," #include \"analyze-has-tpm2.h\""," #include \"analyze-image-policy.h\""," #include \"analyze-inspect-elf.h\"","+#include \"analyze-io-uring-filter.h\""